"EgoBabyVLM: Benchmarking Cross-Modal Learning from Naturalistic Egocentric Video Data | Research - AI at Meta (https://ai.meta.com/research/publications/egobabyvlm-benchmarking-cross-modal-learning-from-naturalistic-egocentric-video-data/)\nciteturn41144view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://ai.meta.com/research/publications/egobabyvlm-benchmarking-cross-modal-learning-from-naturalistic-egocentric-video-data/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 242\nL0: #####\nL1: \nL2: ## Products\nL3: \nL4:   * cite0†Muse L5:   * cite1†Meta AI L6:   * cite2†Media Generation L7:   * cite3†Vibes L8: \nL9: #####\nL10: \nL11: ## AI Research\nL12: \nL13:   * cite4†Overview L14:   * cite5†Projects L15:   * cite6†Resources & Tools L16:   * cite7†Publications L17:   * cite8†GitHub†github.com L18: \nL19: #####\nL20: \nL21: ## Resources\nL22: \nL23:   * cite9†Blog L24:   * cite10†Learning Hub L25:   * cite11†Demos†aidemos.meta.com L26: \nL27: #####\nL28: ## About\nL29: \nL30:   * cite12†Overview L31:   * cite13†Open Source L32:   * cite14†Careers†www.metacareers.com L33: \nL34: * cite15†Products L35: * cite15†AI Research L36: * cite15†Resources L37: * cite15†About L38: * cite16†AI Developers†developer.meta.com L39: * cite17†Try Muse†applink.muse.ai L40: * #### HUMAN & MACHINE INTELLIGENCE\nL41: \nL42: #### RESEARCH\nL43: \nL44: # EgoBabyVLM: Benchmarking Cross-Modal Learning from Naturalistic Egocentric Video Data\nL45: \nL46: May 20, 2026\nL47: ## Abstract\nL48: Children acquire language grounding with remarkable robustness from limited visuo-linguistic input in ways that surpass today's best large multimodal models. Recent research suggests current vision-language models (VLMs) trained on curated web data fail to generalize to the sparse, weakly-aligned egocentric streams produced by wearable devices, embodied agents, and infant head-cams -- and no fixed evaluation pipeline exists for measuring progress on this regime.\nL49: We train VLMs on datasets with varying degrees of semantic alignment between visual and linguistic inputs, including naturalistic infant and adult egocentric videos, and evaluate them with a comprehensive suite spanning multimodal language grounding and unimodal vision and language tasks.\nL50: At the core of this suite is Machine-DevBench, a corpus-grounded benchmark of lexical and grammatical competence, automatically generated from the model's training vocabulary across logarithmic frequency bins to eliminate the train/eval mismatch and low statistical power of prior developmental benchmarks.\nL51: Our results show that current VLM paradigms hinge on the tight semantic alignment of curated data and fail to exploit the weakly-aligned signal that dominates naturalistic egocentric input -- the very regime in which humans thrive. To motivate progress, we introduce the EgoBabyVLM Challenge to drive the development of models capable of grounded language learning from the kind of naturalistic data that human infants experience.\nL52: cite18†Download the Paper†scontent-fra3-1.xx.fbcdn.net L53: #### AUTHORS\nL54: \nL55: Written by\nL56: \nL57: cite19†Dongyan Lin L58: \nL59: Phillip Rust\nL60: \nL61: Angel Villar Corrales\nL62: \nL63: Alvin W. M. Tan\nL64: \nL65: Mahi Luthra\nL66: \nL67: Charles-Eric Saint-James\nL68: \nL69: Rashel Moritz\nL70: \nL71: Sheila Krogh-Jespersen\nL72: \nL73: Vanessa Stark\nL74: \nL75: Surya Parimi\nL76: \nL77: Jiayi Shen\nL78: \nL79: Youssef Benchekroun\nL80: \nL81: Yosuke Higuchi\nL82: \nL83: Martin Gleize\nL84: \nL85: Tom Fizycki\nL86: \nL87: Nicolas Hamilakis\nL88: \nL89: Manel Khentout\nL90: \nL91: Sho Tsuji\nL92: \nL93: Balázs Kégl\nL94: \nL95: cite20†Juan Pino L96: \nL97: Michael C. Frank\nL98: \nL99: Emmanuel Dupoux\nL100: \nL101: Publisher\nL102: \nL103: arXiv\nL104: \nL105: Research Topics\nL106: \nL107: cite21†Human & Machine Intelligence L108: \nL109: cite22†Nat